LogBeamOS (21/11/2026): Wine 11.0 wininet, HttpQueryInfo with HTTP_QUERY_RAW_HEADERS or HTTP_QUERY_RAW_HEADERS_CRLF
and an index above 0 fails with ERROR_HTTP_HEADER_NOT_FOUND, as on Windows. Wine returned the headers for any index,
so a program that reads them with an index until the call fails (WIRES-X 2.010) never left its loop.
Correction by Octávio Filipe Pereira Gonçalves, CT7BFV; found and reported by Bráulio Sousa, CT7APZ (LogBeamOS tester),
November 2026.
Apply with: patch -d wine-11.0 -p1 < wininet-indice.patch

--- a/dlls/wininet/http.c
+++ b/dlls/wininet/http.c
@@ -3706,6 +3706,15 @@
             DWORD len = 0;
             DWORD res = ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER;

+            /* There is only one instance of the raw headers: as on Windows, a higher index is not found.
+             * Programs that enumerate with an index until the call fails (MFC CHttpFile::QueryInfo loops,
+             * such as WIRES-X reading UpdateInfoX_New.bin) never stop otherwise. */
+            if (requested_index > 0)
+            {
+                LeaveCriticalSection( &request->headers_section );
+                return ERROR_HTTP_HEADER_NOT_FOUND;
+            }
+
             if (request_only)
                 headers = build_request_header(request, request->verb, request->path, request->version, TRUE);
             else
@@ -3739,6 +3748,15 @@
             LPWSTR headers;
             DWORD len;

+            /* There is only one instance of the raw headers: as on Windows, a higher index is not found.
+             * Programs that enumerate with an index until the call fails (MFC CHttpFile::QueryInfo loops,
+             * such as WIRES-X reading UpdateInfoX_New.bin) never stop otherwise. */
+            if (requested_index > 0)
+            {
+                LeaveCriticalSection( &request->headers_section );
+                return ERROR_HTTP_HEADER_NOT_FOUND;
+            }
+
